<activity xml:id="activity-determine-if-continuous">
	<title>Describe Definining Traits of Continuity</title>
	<introduction><p>The goal of this activity is to determine traits of functions where they are continuous.</p></introduction>
	<task><p>For each function given in <xref ref="continuousyesno" /> determine where the function is continuous by using examples in <xref ref="continuousyes" /> and <xref ref="continuousno" />. Your response should be intervals where the function is continuous and a set of examples from above that you matched to this function.</p></task>
	<task><p>Based on the example in <xref ref="continuousyes" />, <xref ref="continuousno" />, and <xref ref="continuousyesno" /> describe conditions for continuity. It may be easier to describe discontinuity.</p></task>
	<task><p>Can the limit be defined at a point that is discontinuous?</p></task>
</activity>

